# CODEOWNERS — APP specification repository
#
# This file maps repository paths to the GitHub team(s) from which GitHub
# requests review on a pull request touching those paths.
#
# CODEOWNERS uses LAST-MATCH-WINS semantics. More specific patterns must
# appear LATER in this file to override earlier general ones.
#
# These assignments only REQUEST review. Blocking would come from the
# "Require review from Code Owners" option of the main ruleset
# (main-protection, active since 2026-10-24). That option is off until each
# code-owning team has a member who does not author the pull requests it
# reviews (APP-DEC-0004 §4). Once it is on, an approval from any one listed
# team satisfies a path with several owners. Until then every change needs
# one approval from someone other than the last pusher, plus Release
# Approver sign-off for the classes in GOVERNANCE.md §2.2.
#
# See /GOVERNANCE.md §2.2 for the approval policy that uses these
# assignments.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: any path not matched below gets Release Approver review.
# This covers top-level governance files (LICENSE, README, CONTRIBUTING,
# GOVERNANCE, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, SECURITY, SECURITY-AUTOMATION, CHANGELOG,
# and anything else at the root).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                  @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workflows and CI tooling — custodians own supply-chain concerns.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/**              @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians
/.github/scripts/**                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians
/.github/actions/**                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians
/.github/dependabot.yml            @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians

# CODEOWNERS itself: GitHub requests review from both listed teams. Once
# code-owner review is enforced, an approval from either team satisfies it
# (APP-DEC-0004 §4). Until then a change needs one approval from someone
# other than the last pusher and Release Approver sign-off (.github/** path).
/.github/CODEOWNERS                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# release-approvers.txt: the list of authorised sign-off identities.
# GitHub requests review from both listed teams. Once code-owner review is
# enforced, an approval from either team satisfies it (APP-DEC-0004 §4).
# Until then a change needs one approval from someone other than the last
# pusher and Release Approver sign-off (.github/** path). release-integrity
# reads this file from the base branch, so a PR cannot use its own modified
# version to pass its check.
/.github/release-approvers.txt     @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# Issue forms and PR template: editors maintain them; release-approvers are
# also listed because template changes affect governance signalling. GitHub
# requests review from both listed teams. Once code-owner review is
# enforced, an approval from either team satisfies it (APP-DEC-0004 §4).
# Until then a change needs one approval from someone other than the last
# pusher and Release Approver sign-off (.github/** path).
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/**         @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/.github/pull_request_template.md  @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legal, scope, decisions, releases — Release Approver authority.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/legal/**                          @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/csl/**                            @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/decisions/**                      @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/releases/**                       @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# OPERATIONS-REGISTRY: the record of Apps, Actions, settings and permission
# grants. GitHub requests review from both listed teams. Once code-owner
# review is enforced, an approval from either team satisfies it
# (APP-DEC-0004 §4). Until then a change needs one approval from someone
# other than the last pusher and Release Approver sign-off (a governance
# and CI path, GOVERNANCE.md §2.2).
/OPERATIONS-REGISTRY.md            @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Specification drafts.
# Normative drafts default to editors; APP-1 is elevated to custodians +
# release-approvers because of its constitutional significance.
# CODEOWNERS does not support character ranges such as [0-5], so each
# normative document has its own line. APP-1 is listed separately with
# its elevated owners; it is no longer covered by an editors line.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/drafts/spec/APP-0*                @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/drafts/spec/APP-2*                @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/drafts/spec/APP-3*                @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/drafts/spec/APP-4*                @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/drafts/spec/APP-5*                @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/drafts/spec/APP-1*                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# Informative guides: editors.
/drafts/guides/**                  @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/guides/**                         @agenticprocessprotocol/editors

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Change-impact manifests — editors prepare, release-approvers verify.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/changes/**                        @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accompanying artefacts (informative, outside the Specification).
# Publication clearance is a Release Approver act; editors do technical
# review.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/schemas/**                        @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/reference/**                      @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/tools/**                          @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians

# End of CODEOWNERS.
